---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_50",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 50,
  "text": "<p> [[140.1]] <b>44. HERMANN CONRING AN LEIBNIZ</p>\n<p> [[140.2]] Helmstedt, 16./26. Februar 1671. [40.49.]</b></p>\n<p> [[140.14]] Amplissime et Clar^#'m^#'e Vir. </p>\n<p> [[140.15]] Literae Tuae ut omnes ita etiam quas ultimas dedisti longe mihi sunt gratissimae. Referunt\n[[140.16]] enim ingenium igneum et indefessum nec intra unius alicujus doctrinae angustias sese continens:\n[[140.17]] cujus generis perquam rarae sunt dotes. Adhoc sentio non inter rudes conatus tua\n[[140.18]] consistere, sed jam tum eximios fecisse in omnigena doctrina progressus, idque aetate perquam\n[[140.19]] matura. Deum veneror, uti et vires et seros annos tantis ingenii beneficiis suppares in publicos\n[[140.20]] usus tibi largiatur. Calcaribus non egere te, gaudeo. Quod impetum luxuriantem animi ipsemet\n[[140.21]] velis nonnihil refrenare, laudo plurimum. Et vero ita est. Refrenanda saepenumero sunt magis\n[[140.22]] quam urgenda majora quaevis ingenia: quo et valetudini suae parcant ad annos prolixiores, et\n[[140.23]] consulant famae in perpetuitatem. </p>\n<p> [[140.24]] De tuis prudentiae juris ordinandae rectius studiis sententiam meam dixi jam tum ingenue;\n[[140.25]] nec muto. Nisi scilicet accesserit Regum Principumque auctoritas, nihil effeceris. Quod si\n[[140.26]] tamen solito rectius imbuti fuerint animi eorum, qui Regentibus sunt in consilio, fortassis justa\n[[140.27]] legum constitutio tandem aliquando obtinebit. Tempus autem illius futurae fortunae definire\n[[140.28]] non equidem ausim: imo audeo praedicere, brevi haud licere tale quidquam exspectare. Nihilominus\n[[140.29]] uti tu pergas bene, ceu coepisti, mereri de hoc utilissimo negotio, etiam atque etiam\n[[140.30]] suadeo. </p>\n<p> [[141.1]] Quae de motu in Naturali Philosophia corrigenda censes, ex parte nondum assequor, ex\n[[141.2]] parte autem non possum non improbare. Ne quid scilicet dissimulem, equidem arbitror, id quod\n[[141.3]] tu statuis omnem motum esse localem, infinitis experimentis indies falsi convinci, neque ex\n[[141.4]] antiquo aevo quenquam praeter Democriti scholam tibi suffragari. Quemadmodum vero tellus\n[[141.5]] moveatur ex tua sententia, et quomodo ex ejus motu Oceani fiant reciprocationes, quia nondum\n[[141.6]] docuisti nondum quoque intelligo. Ubi meditamenta tua prodierint in lucem aequum me\n[[141.7]] experieris judicem. Quod si experimentis firmis et justi numeri fueris instructus, laudabo: sin,\n[[141.8]] non potero. Nova quaeque habent facilem imperiti vulgi assensum; sed brevi iterum evanescunt,\n[[141.9]] et a veteris Philosophiae gnaris statim in ipsa janua rejiciuntur, interdum cum <b>risu</b> et\n[[141.10]] quadam ignominia. Anglia hodie circa nova inventa perquam laboriosam sese praestat. Nec ego\n[[141.11]] non plurimum delector illa industria empirica. Hactenus tamen omni illa <greek>ĕmpeiríä</greek> pene nihil\n[[141.12]] novi stabilitum vidi, et Aristotelica dogmata quam multa egregie confirmata: cum tamen boni\n[[141.13]] illi Angli, prae imperitia veteris doctrinae, putaverint plane nova se docere et hactenus observata\n[[141.14]] nemini. Adhoc tantum non omnes illorum laborant <greek>ăpod[e]iktikh̃w</greek> inscitia: vitio scientiis\n[[141.15]] constituendis plurimum adversante: ne quid nunc dicam de ipsamet arte <greek>ĕmpeiríaw.</greek> Non\n[[141.16]] dubito, ea in re rectius te Tibi consulturum. </p>\n<p> [[141.17]] Circa artem medicam noviter factis experimentis quaedam solito felicius hodie doceri et\n[[141.18]] agi posse, omnino et ipse tecum sentio. Quod si autem esses in veterum Medicorum libris\n[[141.19]] versatus, agnosceres quamplura hodie ignorari antiquis cognita. Utrinque scilicet peccatur: <greek>o^%(/i\n[[141.20]] nevterízontew</greek> sola recentia et norunt et admirantur, vetera quaevis superbe fastidiunt, suam\n[[141.21]] inscitiam doctis prodentes: alii vetera sola amplexantur recentium incuriosi. Ego neutris\n[[141.22]] accedo: sed vetera et nova soleo conjungere. Nostra haec aetas avidissima est solarum novitatum,\n[[141.23]] ignara veterum: cum insolente fastu aliorum, et sui stolida quadam <greek>filaytíä</greek>. Quod\n[[141.24]] equidem plurimum doleo: quoniam quantum una parte crescunt tantum altera scientiae quaevis\n[[141.25]] decrescunt. Non dubito, magno cum fructu et doctrinae augmento utramque Te viam calcaturum. </p>\n<p> [[141.27]] Ab Eminentissimo Electore Moguntino Consiliarii aliquod munus concessum tibi gratulor:\n[[141.28]] praesertim quoniam hinc dignitas quidem tibi accessit, studiis tamen nihil detractum. Deus\n[[141.29]] porro faveat eximiis tuis institutis, Leibnizi. Ego sum maneboque\n [[141.30]] Tui semper studiosissimus </p>\n<p> [[141.31]] Raptim Helmestadii 1671 16/26 Febr. H. Conringius. </p>\n<p> [[142.1]] Carmen tuum perplacet. Utinam ex vero fusum sit oraculum! Quae Edsardo et Vogelio\n[[142.2]] destinasti curabo diligenter. Ad omnia Tua respondere vetat temporis angustia. Caeteroquin\n[[142.3]] fuisset gratissimum, de iis tecum nonnihil prolixius conferendi. </p>\n<p> [[142.4]] Amplissimo et Clar^#'m^#'o Viro D. Gotfredo Guilielmo Leibnitio J.U.D. et Consiliario Electorali\n[[142.5]] Moguntino, amico meo pereximio. </p>\n",
  "number": "44.",
  "title": "HERMANN CONRING AN LEIBNIZ",
  "date": "Helmstedt, 16./26. Februar 1671. [40.49.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:44. HERMANN CONRING AN LEIBNIZ Helmstedt, 16./26. Februar 1671. [40.49.] Amplissime et Clar^#'m^#'e Vir. Literae Tuae ut omnes ita etiam quas ultimas dedisti longe mihi sunt gratissimae. Referunt enim ingenium igneum et indefessum nec intra unius alicujus doctrinae angustias sese continens: cujus ge...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>